gue that the  powerful relic that they're all  basically competing for is the blood gem  of ulysses stone now those guys don't  know what the blood gem is this is an  artifact that does grant people the  normal superhero abilities so like super  strength and speed and durability and  stamina yada yada but it also grants  that person immortality and a healing  factor now one of the things to know is  the powers of the gym are not absolute  that a person is able to use the powers  of the gym relative to how much revenge  they have so if this is a person who is  just hell-bent with some sort of  personal vendetta that seeks out revenge  with just the most extreme passion  imaginable they'll be able to utilize  the gem to its full capacity whereas if  it's a person who's just a little pissed  off because a cop gave them a ticket for  rolling through a stop sign even though  they're pretty sure they stopped they'll  be able to use a decent portion of the  gems power something else that i want to  point out here is that among the  different cast members we saw there are  some that we definitively know for sure  one of whom i think is going to blow  your mind of course there's ulysses  bloodstone who is the guy in the coffin  there's elsa bloodstone who's likely  going to be the one to end up getting  the gym at the end i can't imagine why  that wouldn't be the case of course  we've got jack russell who is werewolf  by night we've got the man thing which  really brings in a whole host of other  questions but there is potentially a  wakandan there and that's one of the  coolest things so in marvel comics there  is a group called the monster hunters  which is actually a group led by ulysses  bloodstone and that's exactly who this  group seems to be if that's the case  there is a guy there who has a lightning  shape cut into the side of his head into  his haircut that reminds me of a  character named zawadi who is actually a  woman in the comics zawadi basically had  a scar across her eye which was done in  a lightning bolt fashion i wouldn't be  surprised if that was the case would  would be really interesting to see that  not everybody who is wakandan actually  stayed with wakanda that some defected  off and one of them became a monster  hunter i think it would just be a really  really cool little thing to have going  on there but we won't definitively know  until the show comes out but as far as  the man thing goes this is one of the  most anticipated aspects of the marvel  cinematic universe that i am really  looking forward to but beyond that it  brings in a litany of questions i mean  the role of jack russell a werewolf by  night seems pretty self-explanatory  given the trailer that we saw that  basically he either snuck into the  mansion or is there in the mansion for  any number of reasons that they're going  to reveal that he's basically a werewolf  and it's going to be up to everybody  there to hunt him right maybe he was  invited there you know we want you to  join our band of monster hunters  psych we're gonna hunt you and then he's  just fleeing for his life but with man  thing and really the tva this raises a  litany of questions and here's the  reason why so in marvel comics man thing  is a guy named theo who at one point was  trying to develop a version of the super  soldier serum he basically took the  serum he memorized it tore up the  documents and then through a series of  circumstances basically ended up jumping  into a swamp after injecting himself  with the serum and because of the  properties of the swamp combined with  the serums properties basically turned  him into the man thing and he's not  nearly as smart as he used to be he's  just a giant lumbering beast that moves  around but he guards the portal to the  nexus of realities so if you were to go  to the florida everglades and if you  were to encounter the man thing and you  were to try to pass him and go into the  nexus of realities the man thing would  test you and he would touch you and  that's where everything shifts because  those who feel fear burn at the touch of  the man thing meaning if you're afraid  of him you will literally burn alive and  you see that happen in the trailer the  man thing grabs a guy's head and then  because that guy is scared of the man  thing he basically burns alive his  entire head just totally fries and so if  you pass the test you can enter into the  nexus of realities and then basically  access the multiverse now that principle  right there would justify the existence  of the tva  but nothing else the trailer does  because the  tva we know from just what we saw in the  loki tv show the time variance authority  exists to grab those individuals who  quote unquote leave their predestined  path and then either take them to the  tva headquarters or just wipe them from  existence entirely and then destroy the  entirety of their timeline and that's  basically it again all of that was done  for the purpose of ensuring that no  alternate realities would lead to the  creation of kang now this gives us even  more questions because we don't  definitively know when this show takes  place it's in black and white so we  could argue that maybe it takes place  back in like the 1950s there really  isn't anything in the trailer to  indicate that it takes place in the  modern era a lot of the artifacts that  we see around the mansion look like  artifacts from the 50s or before maybe  even the 60s potentially but it could  also be that this show is just a giant  roost much like wand division was where  it kicks off with the first couple  episodes in black and white it looks  like a 1950s sitcom and then suddenly  you start fast tracking into the modern  era and you find out that it takes place  in the current age if that's the case  the tva is under the control of king the  conqueror again how the tva is involved  here i don't know because they just look  like guards another possibility here is  that it's not actually the tva it just  looks like the tva there's nothing  that's come out that's verified that it  is the time variance authority they just  kind of happen to look like them which  is not an uncommon thing they've  basically got body armor and they've got  helmets to protect them and they look  like advanced military guys and they've  got staffs they could potentially kill  but are most likely used to subdue  people and like that's basically it but  even in that moment in the trailer when  werewolf by night is facing off against  those agents in that giant room when you  look at the lights they look like lights  from the tva headquarters it looks like  tva stuff so i don't definitively know  what this means and even if you look at  the environment that they're in in the  maze when you have that opening scene  right the scene that establishes the  location the drone shot where it's  overhead it doesn't look like it's in a  giant swamp in florida if anything it  looks like it's out in massachusetts or  possibly on bloodstone island so again  it doesn't look like in the traditional  florida everglades location but say for  example that it's not and say for  example that man thing was taken away  from the florida everglades that means  there's no guardian for the portal to  the nexus of all realities now this is  where we could potentially get into like  the final scene of this show one of the  things to remember here is that we're in  the multiverse saga and so most  everything that the marvel cinematic  universe is producing right now pertains  to the multiverse some things don't  she-hulk for example has nothing to do  with the greater multiverse as a whole  but the thing about this is the man  thing is a character that is irrevocably  intertwined with the multiverse which  means it has to have something to do  with that so what if at the end of this  special right what if since the marvel  cinematic universe always ties into  something bigger when it comes to their  shows for example in she-hulk the  incredible hulk has taken off to sakaar  which is probably going to set the stage  for planet hulk and world war hulk what  if this show  directly segues into loki what if we  look at it like a comic book tie-in and  we say this is going to lead into  something else what if with that portal  having no guards whatsoever  what if loki comes out of it at the end  of the show and that gives us or sets  the stage for the loki season 2 show  which is how loki gets back home and  then his whole event transpires from  there what if that's the case what if  that's what happens we get to the very  end of this show and literally it just  kind of transitions to the florida  everglades and it's like the nexus of  realities or access to the multiverse or  they somehow establish that in the show  itself when they talk about the man  thing and loki steps out and then it  just cuts to black what if that happens  i have no clue having said that i do  love that this trailer has a lot of  mystery it gives us virtually nothing in  terms of how it fits into the bigger  picture of the mcu it could be just  completely and totally isolated the  leaks could be true that it just gives  us the show and the show ends and it has  no involvement with anything else  whatsoever outside of setting the stage  for the legion of monsters with like  werewolf by night and man thing  basically teaming up elsa bloodstone  gets the gym and goes and does her thing  or it could have a much larger role in  terms of tying in to loki or potentially  even something else let me know down in  the comment section what you guys think  and let me know how excited you are  about this show but with that being said  guys we're gonna bring this video to an  end make sure you check out our video  here which has all the highlights from  the announcements from d23 in case there  was anything you missed and i will catch  you all later  peace

